# crush treats ollama as a first-class provider TYPE (not plain openai-compat):
# it enumerates the endpoint's /v1/models itself and backfills each model's
# context window from ollama's /api/show. No model add lines, no API key,
# fully offline - the fallback when casper is unreachable or rate-limited.

# To start the server (ollama-app cask) and get a model:
open -a Ollama
ollama pull <model>
ollama list

# To wire it, in ~/.config/crush/crushrc:
#   provider add ollama --type ollama \
#     --base-url "http://127.0.0.1:11434/v1"

# To see exactly what crush will discover:
curl -s http://127.0.0.1:11434/v1/models | jq -r '.data[].id'

# Memory check before pulling anything big: local models are vetted with
# llmfit; anything that fits poorly (>~50% of RAM) is a bad idea.

# To launch on ollama: there is NO --model flag. Either pick once in the TUI -
# command palette (ctrl+p) -> switch model - which persists across sessions,
# or pin the default in crush.json so every launch starts on ollama:
#   "models": {
#     "large": { "provider": "ollama", "model": "<id from ollama list>" },
#     "small": { "provider": "ollama", "model": "<id from ollama list>" }
#   }

# One-shot check that the wiring works end to end:
crush run "say hi"
